## Skill Router

Skills are expected under `~/.cursor/skills/` (or project `.cursor/skills/`). House catalog,
[mattpocock/skills](https://github.com/mattpocock/skills) (allowlist), and
[superpowers](https://github.com/obra/superpowers) (minus denylist) install into the same
directory — see [ADR 0020](../../context/adr/0020-matt-superpowers-hybrid.md).

| Trigger | Skill | Notes |
|---------|-------|-------|
| Commit / "commit this" | `commit` | User-invoked (`/commit`) — hybrid message format |
| Pin domain language, glossary, architectural decision, or architecture fork | `grill-with-docs` | **Default** for forks — drives `grilling` + `domain-modeling`; updates `CONTEXT.md` / ADRs |
| Stateless grill (no working directory / no docs) | `grill-me` | Matt thin wrapper → `grilling` only |
| Front/back or service-to-service boundary that must not drift: OpenAPI, AsyncAPI, JSON Schema, generated types | `contract-first` | Adapted from ECC (MIT) |
| End session / hand work to another agent | `handoff` | User-invoked; save to `<workspace>/.cursor/handoffs/` |
| Terse / token-efficient replies | `caveman` | Levels: lite, full, ultra, wenyan-* (default on via rule) |
| Document a resolved env/tooling fix | `less-trouble` | Writes `docs/troubleshoot/TROUBLESHOOT.md` |
| Curated workspace map before broad exploration | `map-architecture` | Maintains `context/architecture-graph.json` |
| Initialise / standardise repo docs | `init-repo` | User-invoked (`/init-repo`) |
| Which Matt flow fits | `ask-matt` | Router over Matt user-invoked skills |
| Turn conversation into a tracker spec | `to-spec` | After grilling; no interview |
| Split plan into tracer-bullet tickets | `to-tickets` | |
| Implement a ticket or spec | `implement` / `implement-spec` | Drives patched TDD + Matt `code-review` |
| Review since a fixed point | `code-review` | Standards ∥ Spec axes (Matt) |
| Deep modules / deepening survey | `codebase-design` / `improve-codebase-architecture` | Matt |
| Asked whether a skill or skill folder is safe to install | `skill-inspector` | Vendored SkillSpector |
| Any bug, test failure, unexpected behavior | `systematic-debugging` | Superpowers — root cause before fixes |
| Feature or fix with tests first | `test-driven-development` | Superpowers red → green |
| Create or improve a skill | `writing-skills` | Superpowers |
| Write / execute an implementation plan (file-based, non-tracker) | `writing-plans`, `executing-plans`, `subagent-driven-development` | Save to `<workspace>/.cursor/plans/` |
| Ask for or respond to a code review (feedback handling) | `receiving-code-review` | Superpowers; product review is Matt `code-review` |
| About to claim work is done | `verification-before-completion` | Evidence before assertions |
| Isolation, parallel work, closing a branch | `using-git-worktrees`, `dispatching-parallel-agents`, `finishing-a-development-branch` | |

If a task fits a skill above, load and follow that skill. Do not reinvent its process inline.

**`grill-with-docs` vs Superpowers brainstorming:** brainstorming is **not installed**. Architecture
forks and domain work use `grill-with-docs`. Open-ended non-code shaping can still use Matt
`grilling` / `grill-me` without inventing a parallel design-doc skill.

